PegResponsiveExponentialIrm::setPegOracle(address)
├── given caller is not the current owner
│   └── it should reject before validation or checkpointing, including pending owners
└── given caller is the current owner
    ├── when newOracle is zero
    │   └── it should reject before checkpointing
    └── when newOracle is nonzero
        ├── given market is unbound
        │   └── it should skip market queries and accrual
        ├── given market is paused
        │   └── it should query the exact PAUSE_TYPE and skip accrual
        ├── given market is active
        │   ├── it should accrue exactly once using the old oracle
        │   └── it should roll back all effects if the pause query or market accounting fails
        ├── it should emit SetPegOracle and install the new source
        ├── it should reset prior recovery confirmation and sample the new source
        ├── when the new observation is valid
        │   ├── it should immediately apply its effective rate
        │   └── it should preserve hysteresis and restart qualifying recovery
        ├── when the new observation is invalid or reverts
        │   └── it should hold the bounded rate and stress mode with recovery cleared
        ├── when the new address has no code
        │   └── the typed read should revert and roll back replacement
        ├── when the new source equals the current source
        │   └── it should still checkpoint, emit replacement, and refresh
        ├── it should preserve the accrual timestamp when paused or unbound
        └── it should emit BorrowRateUpdated and IRStateUpdated after the setter and stress events
